# Build context pruning for the SDK image build.
#
# core/ is not itself a Docker build context. It is passed to the sdk/ build as
# a BuildKit NAMED context:
#
#     docker build --build-context core=../core -f sdk/dockerfiles/Dockerfile sdk/
#
# BuildKit applies this file to that named context, which is the only reason it
# exists here. Without it the context is 1.4 GB, essentially all of it
# tests/external/repos -- vendored checkouts of oil, cpython, coreutils, grep
# and friends that the image build has no use for. With it, 3.8 MB.
tests/
build/
*.gcov

# Nothing below is needed to compile the binary.
docs/
*.md
.git/
.github/
